Required target contract

Distinguish these identities explicitly:

Installation initiator

The installation command may be initiated by:

* the configured NPID;
* an approved deployment/service account;
* an explicitly authorized administrator for bootstrap or recovery.

The initiator is not automatically required to be the target NPID.

Runtime owner

The installed application files, runtime directories and normal application process must belong to and run as the environment’s configured NPID.

For DEV, current owner-supplied evidence identifies:

tclue999devs

Do not hard-code that DEV account into PAT or Production.

PAT and Production must obtain their NPID values from their own deployment profiles. Unknown values must remain explicit blockers.

Privilege behavior

Normal installation must not:

* ask for the owner’s personal password;
* use interactive sudo;
* use sudo -S;
* use sudo -i;
* use su -;
* use sshpass, expect or SUDO_ASKPASS;
* persist credentials;
* grant broad root access.

All automated privileged commands must use a previously approved noninteractive path such as narrowly scoped sudo -n.

If an approved noninteractive privilege path is absent, fail before modifying the installation root and report:

PASSWORDLESS_PRIVILEGE_PREREQUISITE_MISSING

Do not weaken controls merely to allow any user to install.

Important semantic rule

“NPID is not required to invoke the installer” must not become any of the following:

* NPID ownership is optional;
* the application runs under the invoking user;
* an arbitrary user may select an arbitrary owner;
* host or account validation is bypassed;
* /app/clue becomes writable by broad groups or everyone;
* the installer silently falls back to the current user;
* DEV identity is reused for PAT or Production;
* root becomes the normal runtime owner.

The target NPID must come from the selected environment deployment profile, not from an unrestricted command-line value.

